# VER31 release signers (code/specs/VER31-tiered-release-standard.md, section 9.1).
#
# OpenSSH allowed_signers format, one hardware-backed key per line:
#
#   <principal> namespaces="git,coding-adventures-statement,coding-adventures-buckets,coding-adventures-signers" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA... <comment>
#
# Only security-key (sk-*) key types are accepted, and only the `namespaces=`
# option (OpenSSH's allowed_signers has no `verify-required`; the gate checks
# the signature's user-presence and user-verification flags itself).
#
# This file is a signed chain. It is a placeholder until the owner adds the
# first key together with this line, unindented and without the leading "#   ":
#
#   # revision: 1
#
# That version is the trust anchor, and every release's notes print it. Every
# later version must raise the number by one and be
# committed with .github/release-signers.sig, signed
# (ssh-keygen -Y sign -n coding-adventures-signers) by a key of the PREVIOUS
# version. The gate reads this file only from main, never from a tagged tree.
#
# Until a key is here, every release is refused (dry runs still work).
